        "original_id": "1d22bb81-5598-5dd3-af20-8b47162cc47f",
        "text": "This chunk explains the concept of independent cities in the United States and identifies St. Louis as one example.\n\nThis chunk is about:\n- Concepts: independent city\n- Places: United States, St. Louis, Missouri, Mississippi River, Illinois\n\nFacts:\n- In the United States, an independent city is a city that is not in the territory of any county or counties, with some exceptions.\n- St. Louis is an independent city in the state of Missouri.\n- St. Louis is a major U.S. port built along the western bank of the Mississippi River on the border with Illinois.",
